From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: validate ingress L3 flow identity

Bind router MACs and PPPoE physical/virtual ingress sessions with verified
transactions. Share physical-port L3 detachment across tagged VLANs and
reserve an untagged fallback outside bridge/tagged allocations. Restore
the original port binding only after its last VLAN leaves.

Consume ingress S/C tags while selecting the VLAN VSI/L3, and restore
software-required tags on CPU egress. Preserve dual-slot identity and
source checks. Write complete XLT rows in ascending QSDK word order and
verify rule/action readback; retain dependencies when withdrawal fails.

For tagged PPPoE, make the VLAN VSI select the session's terminating L3,
as on the routed WAN path in PR #24806. Use that same L3 for the flow
source check. Retain a router-MAC reference with the session, verify VSI
selection, and restore ordinary VLAN routing before clearing session L3.
Reject a second session or mixed plain-IP flow on an owned VSI instead
of silently redirecting an existing routing identity. Physical and QCA
VP sessions retain their independent ingress selection.

Keep XLT/L3 counters, full row readback and existing bounded code-89
diagnostics. Expose the selected PPPoE VSI/L3 and per-stage failure/errno
histograms on demand. Hardware validation of tagged PPPoE remains pending.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
